# T_SCRR: restore.  Esc at the directory prompt sends nothing; the
# question names the directory and says the data is replaced; N sends
# nothing; a directory without a backup is refused (200 naming DIR, the
# client's text); then the restore from BAK succeeds (the test's
# answer).  The requests are checked by T_SCRR.
K ESC ESC
T old
K ENTER
S RESTOREQ
T N
S DECLINED
K ESC
T nosuch
K ENTER
T Y
S NOBACKUP
K ESC
T bak
K ENTER
T Y
S RESTORED
K ESC
